From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cli: key topology radio trees by name

The topology renderer assumes RadioList is always child index two in both a
device and its nested child record.  That ordering is not an API contract and
the current controller tree places another field there.  The live model still
contains 5 devices, 15 radios and 50 BSS records, while `/api/v1/topology`
therefore emits empty haulTypes and edges with band -1/channel 0.  The WebUI
consequently loses every 2.4/5/6 GHz bubble despite a complete mesh.

Resolve RadioList by key, as the newer client and BSS API adapters already do.
This changes presentation only; it neither changes the controller model nor
invents band data when RadioList is genuinely absent.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/rdkb-cli/main.go | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -4759,7 +4759,8 @@ func loadTopologyFromDeviceTree(w  http.ResponseWriter) {
             return
         }
 
-        radioList := parseRadioList(deviceNode.child[2])
+        radioTree := getNetworkTreeByKey(deviceNode, "RadioList")
+        radioList := parseRadioList(radioTree)
         haulTypes := buildHaulTypes(radioList)
 
         backhaulMacAddr := getTreeValue(backhaulTree, "MACAddress")
@@ -4818,7 +4819,8 @@ func loadTopologyFromDeviceTree(w  http.ResponseWriter) {
             channel := 0
 
             // parse the band with extender connected
-            band, channel = getBandAndChannelFromRadioTree(child.child[2])
+            childRadioTree := getNetworkTreeByKey(child, "RadioList")
+            band, channel = getBandAndChannelFromRadioTree(childRadioTree)
 
            edges = append(edges, map[string]interface{}{
                "from":     deviceID,
-- 
